# Most patterns below have no slash in them, so git matches them at every level:
# the root, apps/*, and packages/* alike. The few that do contain a slash are
# anchored to this directory and are grouped at the bottom, where they are
# called out.

# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

# Dependencies and build output
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Caches
.turbo
.cache
*.tsbuildinfo

# The reserved prefix for scratch material — a verification harness, a throwaway
# probe, anything a run writes into a workspace rather than anything anyone
# authored. No slash, so it holds at every level, and the trailing wildcard lets a
# harness name itself (`.scratch-plugin-verify/`). Reserved because untracked
# scratch material is not inert: it joins `eslint .` and `prettier --check .` and
# fails them for the whole package until someone deletes it, and the ESLint half
# reports a syntax error against a file whose syntax is fine. Naming the prefix
# once means the next harness only has to be put in the right place rather than
# added to three lists. The matching entries are `globalIgnores` in
# packages/cli/eslint.config.js — not derived from this file — and that package's
# .prettierignore, since Prettier reads only the .gitignore in its own working
# directory and there is none there. The mechanism is written out beside the
# `files:` list in that ESLint config.
.scratch*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
# ...but the templates are the documentation for what each one is.
!.env.example
# ...and apps/editor/.env.production is opted in, because it is not a secret
# and it is not local. It holds the one address the deployed editor calls,
# which Vite freezes into the published bundle, so it is public by the time
# anyone loads the site. Committing it is what stops a developer's `.env`
# reaching a production build — Vite ranks `.env.production` above `.env` — and
# it is the file apps/editor/scripts/check-deployable-bundle.ts checks the
# built artefact against. A `.env.production.local` is still ignored, which is
# how you build against a local worker without touching this.
!.env.production

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Claude Code working files, at any level
.claude
.claude-src
.claude-design/
CLAUDE.md
V2.md

# Playwright. These are anchored, and correctly so: only apps/editor runs
# Playwright, and it sits at the same depth it did in the web repository.
apps/editor/test-results/
apps/editor/playwright-report/
apps/editor/blob-report/
apps/editor/.playwright/

# wrangler local state
.wrangler

# The CLI's private working notes, all but two of them. This pattern contains a
# slash, so it is anchored to this file's directory — which is why it had to be
# re-pointed at packages/cli when the CLI moved a level down. Left as `todo/*`
# it would have matched nothing and committed every note.
packages/cli/todo/*
!packages/cli/todo/TODO.md
!packages/cli/todo/TODO-completed.md

# Four files the unanchored CLAUDE.md and V2.md rules above would otherwise
# swallow. The root CLAUDE.md is new rather than moved: agents start a session
# at the root, and until it existed nothing there pointed them at the CLI's
# documentation map. The other three — the CLI's own working instructions, its
# V2 design note, and one compiler test fixture — were tracked at the repository
# root for the whole of the CLI's history, so being tracked already those rules
# never applied to them; the merge moved them a level down, where the rules do
# match, fresh, so each needs naming here. The fixture is read from disk by
# compiler.test.ts; CI clones fresh, so leaving it uncommitted fails the CLI
# suite. All four are anchored to their exact paths — the root file by a leading
# slash, since an unanchored !CLAUDE.md would un-ignore every one in the tree —
# so every other CLAUDE.md and V2.md in the repository stays ignored.
!/CLAUDE.md
!packages/cli/CLAUDE.md
!packages/cli/V2.md
!packages/cli/src/cli/lib/__tests__/fixtures/stacks/default/CLAUDE.md

# The Skill Olympics corpus (todo plan CLI-729, was D-162), excluded outright — the plan and
# its 879 supporting files both. `contestants/` is third-party skill text copied
# verbatim from other authors, and `arena/` and `test-cases/` hold the outputs
# those skills produced, the artefacts the benchmark's rubric scores. This
# pattern contains a slash, so it is anchored to this file's directory.
#
# The root .prettierignore names those same three subdirectories, for a related
# reason rather than the same one: reformatting them would rewrite the evidence
# being measured. It is deliberately left as it is — a gitignored file can still
# be formatted locally, so the two rules do different jobs and neither replaces
# the other.
#
# CLI-729 is a live item, so todo/cli.md is written to match: it gives the plan
# and catalog as plain paths rather than links and says outright that they exist
# only on the maintainer's machine. Turning them back into links would ship a
# tracker whose references resolve for one person and nobody else.
todo/plans/CLI-729-skill-olympics/

# generated by packages/cli/scripts/handrun.mjs — the hand-run bundle must sit beside the
# e2e helpers so CLI_ROOT, derived from import.meta.url, still resolves to the package root
packages/cli/e2e/helpers/handrun.gen.mjs
